    "description": "East Syriac martyr, opponent of the Magi, per Maclean's own description. Confirmed at this date by three independent sources: Maclean 1894 ('Raban Pithiun, martyr, opponent of the Magi'), the ACOTE Diocese of Western Europe 2026 calendar ('St. Pithyon'), and the ACOE Diocese of California 2026 calendar ('Mar Rabban Pethyon the Martyr, with Mar Tahmazgard of Beth Slokh'). The identity id was previously scattered across five different unsourced dates (Aug.2, Jul.8, Sept.28, Nov.15, Dec.1) with no citation for any of them -- all stripped.",
